    claim "C3" from-slice="TS.260820.18" state="met-in-part" \
        text="a resolved symptom cannot silently return to present" \
        settled-by="a negative test reverting a resolution without a new frame or an amendment" \
        evidence="tests/symptoms.rs::a_withdrawn_claim_leaves_the_symptom_present_and_the_record_clean \
            — a withdrawal that records `previously-claimed` and `withdrawn-because` passes, and the \
            withdrawal this repository performed on its own S1 is the worked example" \
        residue="nothing REFUSES a silent revert. A symptom edited from resolved back to present \
            with no `previously-claimed` is accepted, because the check has no memory of what the \
            record said before. Recorded as AG3" \
        note="the honest position: this settles that a withdrawal CAN be recorded, not that an \
            unrecorded one is caught"

    decision "the unverifiable claim is withdrawn, not grandfathered" \
        chose="move S1 to `present` and record previously-claimed and withdrawn-because" \
        over="a grandfather clause exempting claims made before the delivery graph existed" \
        because="the narrowing may well have happened. The problem is that nobody can check, and \
            this frame's whole argument is that an assertion nobody can check is not evidence. A \
            method that exempts its own progress reports from the standard it sets is the root cause \
            with a nicer surface" \
